 "requested_at": "2026-11-13T20:08:29.839611Z",
 "text": "Under subsection 26(2) of the *Residential Tenancies Act, 2006*, a landlord is permitted to enter a rental unit without written notice between 8 a.m. and 8 p.m. if the tenancy agreement requires the landlord to clean the unit at regular intervals and the entry is made in accordance with the times specified in the agreement. Because the clause specifies regular intervals (every second Friday) and an entry window between 8 a.m. and 8 p.m. (10 a.m. to 2 p.m.) for cleaning, it complies directly with this statutory exception to the standard 24-hour written notice requirement.\n\nVerdict: enforceable\nSection: 26",
